        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Reject case-colliding skill package files",
        "body": "Closes #575.\n\nRejects case-colliding skill package files consistently across CLI, web upload, API publish, server publish, and GitHub import discovery. Multipart uploads now reject collisions before blob storage and clean up stored blobs if later payload parsing fails; owned GitHub repo discovery filters colliding tree and code-search candidates before listing them as importable.\n\nProof:\n- Real CLI publish on head `dc0539ae61ab` used a case-sensitive APFS fixture containing both `SKILL.md` and `skill.md`; it exited 1 before registry/upload with `Error: Remove case-colliding SKILL.md files: skill.md, SKILL.md.`.\n- Web upload render proof passed for showing `Remove case-colliding SKILL.md files` beside the upload input and keeping the Publish button disabled.\n- API multipart publish with `SKILL.md` plus `skill.md` returns the same collision error before blob storage: `storage.store.calls=0`, `storage.delete.calls=0`.\n- GitHub import discovery on a zip with one valid skill and two colliding candidates returned only the valid `alpha/SKILL.md` candidate.\n- GitHub Actions on the pushed head have 23 passing non-Vercel checks; the remaining Vercel check is blocked on OpenClaw Foundation team authorization.",
